          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best protein powder brands share habits rather than a style: they certify the products you actually buy, disclose exactly what is in the scoop, keep a clean track record and avoid overpromising. Optimum Nutrition and Dymatize lead mainstream whey, Thorne and Klean Athlete lead on sports certification, Transparent Labs and Naked Nutrition lead on transparency, and Garden of Life stands out for certified plant protein. Several big names share parent companies, so the logo tells you less than it seems.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Use brands to build a shortlist, then judge each product on its own label: protein per serving against serving size, cost per 25 g of protein, the ingredient order and a certification you have verified in the certifier's database. That approach works for any brand, including ones not on this page and the house brands on the warehouse shelf.
